    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), which is the handler for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. Added a guard in `addOwner`, placed right after `normalizeNewOwner` (which defaults a missing `registrationDate` to today), so the check sees the canonical registration date:\n   ```java\n   if (dailyLimitReached(owner.getRegistrationDate())) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n   }\n   ```\n2. Added a `dailyLimitReached(LocalDate)` helper that counts existing owners sharing that registration date and returns `true` at 100 or more \u2014 mirroring the existing `cityIsAtCapacity` style.\n\nWhen 100+ owners already carry today's `registrationDate`, the next create is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**. The acceptance test (`coreRejectsOverDailyLimit`: create 100, expect the 101st rejected) and the full suite pass.",
